PianoCamera is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE): piano's two cameras (backlog B11). What it takes from other
work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoTorch/PianoTorch.cpp (sha256 c4c761fccfb0f66bfed228c876d20d8f77fbccb3891fc2c91ddf220b1a4a4b40) and
  package/PianoBluetooth/PianoBluetooth.cpp (sha256 91ad1ed3f14ebf37c9c2e0fcd7aeca5df94c438c2913df466b151c508131fa5c): the kext's
    shape (probe gate on the boot argument, a thread, the post-mortem stage word, pages mapped uncached on demand and loaded with an
    explicit ldr, the SPMI observer windows, the cmd-db copy, the lock words' compare-exchange with its 10 us steps, the DRV-2 mapping),
    re-written for this driver.
  package/PianoBluetooth/BtRpmh.h (sha256 e5c33751acf1a043685fa14367cbe1334a6694d0aa2d434a2cc4e397e2c75eea): copied as CameraRpmh.h
    with the namespace and the command type changed (the VRM transaction on apps DRV-2; the same sequence as PianoWifi's vrmLocked).
  package/PianoKeyboard/BitI2c.h (sha256 c63c87803997d89a4a09be877d7f04712e5d02e3d00bae30f41bb288beb76767): copied as BitI2c.h with
    the namespace, include guard and header comment changed, the code unchanged (the software I2C master).
  package/PianoKeyboard/CmdDb.h (sha256 794cf39c76e2c903d79cc1146ae25d946946862daa9b8848d616e9ad8107c716) and
  package/PianoPower/SpmiObserver.h (sha256 4805d4fb7af91c210d75b9791e125f3789b7671e895afe6f80af27a36a849b07): included, not copied.
  package/PianoVideo/VideoPower.h (sha256 871cd834c9bb422e3fd9aa93cfd087a0c84efa1ee0fee3f4f8c4a17ab878e531) and
  package/PianoVideo/VideoSurvey.h (sha256 a2ca231576ecd9f824d53a63198141ad987d99313075d417531efb05a2e8d4f2): the approach (a GDSC's
    on/off with its CFG completion bits, the shared RCG switch with the root forced on, the clock controller read only behind its GCC
    AHB, the SMMU groups of a stream range), re-expressed in CameraPower.h and CameraSurvey.h.
  package/include/PianoWcnRails.h: the rail rules (read the PMIC first, vote mode/voltage/enable in one transaction, read back, withdraw
    only the enables this driver added, mode and set point left), re-expressed in CameraPower.h for rails no other driver uses.
  package/include/PianoPowerContract.h: the power-tree join.
  The sensor tables in data/camera (data only; their provenance is data/camera/README.md) are read by the host tests through the
    header tooling/camera/sensor-tables.py generates; the kext uses them from level 3 on.

The piano boot DT (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb, sha256 50636effb5f54306ec0ab9a3061cd163d7f003d8797e04585a33205918856840): the camera
clock controllers' places and power domains, cci@ac7b000, isp@ad27000, the camera rails and their consumers, the TLMM reserved ranges.

